'''The Aku Realms''' (魔界編 ''[[wikipedia:ja:魔界|Makai]]-hen'', lit. "'''Demon World Arc'''" or "'''Devil World Arc'''") is a special area unlocked after completing [[The Gates of Aku|Unleashing the Cats]], which in turn requires [[Wicked Cat]], [[Wicked Tank]], and [[Wicked Axe]] to be cleared. To access this unique chapter, tap the spinning portal button labelled "The Aku Gates" above the [[Empire of Cats]] chapter. The Aku Realms were added in [[Version 10.9 Update|update 10.9]].[[File:Theakugates.png|thumb|right|"The Aku Gates" button]]

==Story==
Thanks to the [[Empress' Research]], the [[Cat Units|Cats]] successfully open the gates to another plane of existence. As expected, these lands are dominated by the nefarious [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku Enemies]] they had previously run into, but are also dotted with evil "[[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altars]]" whose magics weaken the Cats to near-powerless levels. As they soon discover, these Altars were the work of a malevolent priest with frightening power and a dastardly plot nine years in the making—"[[High Priest Mamon|Mamon]]", who works tirelessly to undo the seals placed by legendary heroes on the god of destruction—"[[Lord of Ruin Jagando|Jagando]]", in times long past.

Although weakened to critical levels, the Cats battle it out through the Aku Realms and regain their former power little by little, one Altar at a time. Midway through, they reach [[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)|Mount Aku]] ([[wikipedia:Mount Fuji|Mount Fuji]] in the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese Version]]), where Mamon attacks them and makes off with the mountain's "crystal of awakening" needed for the final step of his plan. The Cats catch up to him and defeat him once more on the [[Moon (Aku Realm)|Moon]] ([[:wikipedia:Iriomote Island|Iriomote Island]] in the Japanese Version), only for him to escape once more and the Cats to learn that Jagando has already been revived on Mount Aku/Mount Fuji. But even the god of destruction is no match for an army of weird cats, and with Jagando defeated once more, Mamon loses everything he had worked so hard for, his spirit utterly crushed to where, for the first time in forever, he can finally get his mind off world domination and reunite with his family. The Aku Altars' powerful seals are universally [[Inactive Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|deactivated]], giving the Cats full reign in [[Imminent Disaster|other]] [[Aku's Melody (Merciless)|areas]] where they may have obstructed their progress.

As the Cats leave the Aku Realms, the Lord of Ruin's [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|egg]] in their paws, Mamon parts them farewell and sends them thanks for giving him the chance to rehabilitate, but ends his message on an ominous note: "We'll surely meet again, Battle Cats. Just you wait..."

