==Explanation==
This is basically a bonus chapter of [[Empire of Cats]], with its own map and stages, but there are some catches. First, the stages become available out of order, with [[Korea (Aku Realm)|Korea/Nagasaki]] always being the first, but after that, some stages are randomly chosen to temporarily become available for roughly 3 hours, after which new stages are picked and those that were not completed become unavailable again. Those that were completed stay available forever (with the exception of the [[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)/Invasion|invasion]] on Mount Aku/Mount Fuji). Tap the "Aku Altar Appears!" button at the stage select screen to move immediately to the first of the currently available Aku Altar stages. Tapping the same button again will take you to the next available stage. [[File:E 574.png|250px|thumb|right|The Aku Altar]]
The main gimmick of the Aku Realms is the [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]] and its ability to <u>restrict unit levels</u>. Cats are initially reverted to level 1 (only during [[Battle|battle]]) and have their + levels invalidated. After beating Korea/Nagasaki, the restriction will rise to level 2 for whichever stage to play next, then increases by one after first clearing that next stage and so on. This continues until the 49th stage is beaten and the level restriction reaches 50, with + levels staying disabled all the way. The order of the stages in the map is irrelevant for this; whichever stage you play sixth will be the one in which your cats will be forced to level 6 and so on. This means that it would be optimal to play the stages in order (by waiting for the next to be randomly picked as one of the available stages), as most of the stages are generally in order from easiest to hardest on the map, as one would expect. Not doing so may result in level 10 units having to be used in a stage balanced for level 20 ones, then maybe, level 40 units being available for one of the very first five stages, which would therefore be a free win.

Note that the units used will still keep their current form, meaning that the level restriction only affects the starting stats ([[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]], for example, will revert to level 1, but stay in [[True Form]], so its stats will be higher than a level 1 Tank Cat).

===Stages and Rewards===
The Aku Realms' stages take place in the same locations as normal, but there is one added stop which appears as stage 30: [[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)|Mount Aku/Mount Fuji]], increasing the total number of stages to 49. This stage drops an Aku [[Catfruit]] when cleared for the first time. After completing the [[Moon (Aku Realm)|Moon/Iriomote]] stage, you will receive a one-time Gold Catfruit and unlock an [[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)/Invasion|invasion]] in Mount Aku/Mount Fuji, where you will encounter [[Lord of Ruin Jagando]]. Complete the invasion to receive a [[Platinum Capsules (Gacha Event)|Platinum Ticket]], unlock [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando Jr.]], and strip the Aku Altar of its ability to disable + levels.

[[Treasure]]s still take effect here, but there are no new ones to collect.

===Aku Enemies===
As its name suggests, the Aku Realms are home to a variety of [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku Enemies]], some of which cannot be found elsewhere.
*[[Aku Doge]]
*[[Sinner Snache]]
*[[Cerberus Kids]]
*[[Condemned Peng]]
*[[Aku Gory]]
*[[Le'Behemoth]]
*[[Fallen Bear]]
*[[Wicked Face]]
*[[Dark Priest Mamon]]: Appears in stage 30, [[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)|Mount Aku/Mount Fuji]].
*[[High Priest Mamon]]: Appears in stage 49, [[Moon (Aku Realm)|Moon/Iriomote]].
*[[Lord of Ruin Jagando]]: Appears in the bonus stage, [[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)/Invasion|Mount Aku/Mount Fuji Invasion]].

The strength magnifications vary for each Aku, starting out low but reaching endgame levels in the last few stages.

===Appearance Pattern===
Every 2 hours and 59 minutes, new stages are selected in a randomized process with parameters dependent on the Level Seal. The game will choose up to 5 random stages and then roll the die for each one; if successful, the stage will become available, and if not, the game will try again after another 2 hours and 59 minutes. The number of candidates and possible range of stages that can be chosen are based on the player's current Level Seal. This means that stages near the end of the Aku Realms are effectively locked behind the Level Seal.

